#: ../../source/end-user-guide/access/client-availability.rst:201
msgid "What feature quality levels does Mattermost have?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/access/client-availability.rst:203
msgid ""
"We strive to release viable features. This means that we put in a "
"significant amount of effort to ensure we solve a use case with a high "
"bar for quality. A feature that's viable and meets our criteria for our "
"production quality levels will be released to production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/access/client-availability.rst:205
msgid ""
"However, when working on large and complex features or new products, we "
"may need to test them with a high volume of customers and users. For "
"these scenarios, we'll release them as :ref:`Experimental "
"<administration-guide/manage/feature-labels:experimental>` or :ref:`Beta "
"<administration-guide/manage/feature-labels:beta>`, and implement feature"
" flags and/or A/B testing to validate the effectiveness of features prior"
" to production-level release. Additionally, we `dogfood our features "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eating_your_own_dog_food>`_ on our "
"community server, and provide many configuration options that ensure "
"customers can opt-in when trying experimental or beta features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/access/client-availability.rst:207
msgid ""
"See the :doc:`Mattermost feature labels </administration-guide/manage"
"/feature-labels>` documentation for details on the status, maturity, and "
"support level of each feature, and what you can expect at each level."
msgstr ""

